===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{senseid|en|specific to a particular discipline}} Specifically related to a particular [[discipline]].
#: {{syn|en|technic#Adjective}}
#: {{ux|en|Particle physics uses the word ''spin'' in a '''technical''' sense.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=John Fritze|title=Supreme Court agrees to decide if Trump may end birthright citizenship|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/12/05/politics/supreme-court-agrees-to-hear-birthright|date=2025-12-05|passage=By granting the appeal, the court is directly taking on the merits of a controversy that it largely avoided earlier this year, when it sided with Trump on '''technical''' grounds dealing with how the challenges to the policy were handled by lower courts.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260411164900/https://www.cnn.com/2025/12/05/politics/supreme-court-agrees-to-hear-birthright|archivedate=11 April 2026}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} difficult to understand for those not specialized in this discipline.
##* {{quote-web|en|date=April 22, 2025|author=Artem S. Tashkinov|work=Why Linux is not ready for the desktop (the final edition)|url=https://itvision.altervista.org/why.linux.is.not.ready.for.the.desktop.final.html#Accidental_Desktop_Linux_security|text=This part of the article is going to be quite '''technical''' but I cannot avoid it. It's a very complex topic.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260828115921/https://itvision.altervista.org/why.linux.is.not.ready.for.the.desktop.final.html|archivedate=28 August 2026}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Asaf Darr|title=Selling Technology|page=94|passage=One example of the blurring of boundaries is the growing interdependence of social and '''technical''' skills. The sales engineers and the clients' engineers are all knowledge workers.}}
# {{senseid|en|technological}} Of or related to [[technology]].
#: {{syn|en|technological|technologic}}
#: {{ux|en|Since the 1940s there had been many '''technical''' advancements, and a Mach 3 interceptor was no longer a mere pipe dream.}}
# {{senseid|en|technically minded, adept with science and technology}} {{lb|en|of a person}} Technically minded; adept with science and technology.
#: {{ux|en|Kayla can probably get the printer working. She's '''technical''' like that.}}
# {{senseid|en|Technique related}} Relating to, or requiring, technique.
#: {{syn|en|technic#Adjective}}
#: {{ux|en|The performance showed '''technical''' virtuosity, but lacked inspiration.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Robert Dineen|title=Kings of the Road: A Journey into the Heart of British Cycling|passage=Its design apparently made for interesting racing, with a challenging climb, '''technical''' bends and a finishing straight long enough to produce exciting sprints.}}
## {{senseid|en|requiring advanced techniques}} Requiring advanced techniques for successful completion.
##: {{collocation|en|'''technical''' climbing}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=The Naked Mountaineer: Misadventures of an Alpine Traveler|url=https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0803248792|author=Stephen C. Sieberson|year=2014|passage=It was a '''technical''' ascent involving ropework, belays, and protection, and the exposure was great, but there were abundant hand and footholds, and the rock was sound.}}
# {{senseid|en|not fundamental, in securities and other markets}} {{lb|en|securities and other markets}} Relating to the internal mechanics of a market rather than more basic factors.
#: {{ux|en|The market had a '''technical''' rally, due to an oversold condition.}}
# {{senseid|en|technical versus meaningful}} In the strictest sense, but not practically or meaningfully.
#: {{ux|en|Crossing the front lawn of that house to get to the mailbox was a '''technical''' trespass.}}

